sensitive; same values as search_symbols / find_implementations / get_type_hierarchy / find_callers kindFilter) restricts reported locations to reference sites whose enclosing symbol (the same site accessibilityFilter / nameFilter judge) has that kind (methods, constructors, and property/event accessors are Method; a field initializer is Field; a property definition is Property; top-level statements, enclosed by the synthesized <Main>$, are namespace-level and never match any kind, including Method; a site inside a delegate's Invoke/BeginInvoke/EndInvoke/.ctor is classified as the delegate itself, so it matches Delegate, not Method), applied before maxResults; staticFilter (optional boolean) set to true keeps only locations whose reference site (the same enclosing site symbol accessibilityFilter / nameFilter / kindFilter judge; definition locations judged by the declared symbol itself) is static (ISymbol.IsStatic: static methods, static constructors, operators, static properties / events and their accessors, static and const fields, static types) and false keeps only instance sites (omit = all). Edge rules: a site in a member's signature (a field's, property's, or event's type, or a method's return or parameter types) is judged on the containing type, not the member, so public static App.T Field2; in an instance class, or the return type of public static T Make() in a non-static class, is kept by false, and true misses static-member signatures; attributes and attribute arguments on a member (e.g. [DefaultValue(T.Base)] on a static method) and a cref in a member's doc comment are likewise judged on the containing type; an attribute, attribute argument, or cref on a type declaration is judged on that type; a nested type's base list is judged on the outer type; a method's type-parameter constraint is judged on the method, while a top-level type's type-parameter constraint and a top-level type's base list are namespace-level and never match; nameof and default parameter values are judged on the method; local functions (static or not, including a non-static local function in a static method) and lambdas (including static lambdas) are judged on the member declaring them; a finalizer is instance; an indexer is instance (C# has no static indexers); a site in a custom event accessor follows the event's staticness; an auto-property initializer is judged on the compiler backing field <P>k__BackingField, which shares the property's staticness; a const initializer that references another const is static; members of a nested type are judged on their own staticness, not the containing type's; a site inside a delegate's synthesized members is judged on the delegate type (never static); top-level statements, including top-level local functions, are namespace-level and never match either value, as are using aliases and a namespace's own declaration. Same IsStatic test as get_symbol_info / get_document_outline / search_symbols / find_callers / find_implementations / get_diagnostics staticFilter, but the sites differ from find_callers: find_callers counts top-level statements as static (<Main>$ is kept by true) while find_references never matches them; find_callers judges a local function as its own calling symbol while find_references judges it on the declaring member; both judge an auto-property initializer on the backing field <P>k__BackingField; signature, attribute, cref, constraint, and base-list sites have no find_callers counterpart (they are not calls). get_diagnostics also looks local functions and lambdas through to the declaring member and never matches top-level statements, but judges a declaration-attached site (a member's return or parameter type, an attribute on a member, or a doc-comment cref) on that member, not the containing type, and judges a top-level type's base list and type-parameter constraints on that type rather than as namespace-level. The target symbol's own staticness is irrelevant. Combined with the other filters (all must match) and applied before maxResults; a non-boolean value is rejected with an error (the MCP tool reports INTERNAL_ERROR); sourceFile still locates the target symbol");
        r.RegisterQuery<FindCallersOperation, FindCallersParams, FindCallersResult>(
