ly call sites whose calling symbol is static (ISymbol.IsStatic: static methods, static constructors, operators, static property bodies, static field and const initializers) and false keeps only call sites whose calling symbol is an instance member (omit = all; same IsStatic test as get_symbol_info / get_document_outline / search_symbols / find_implementations staticFilter, but find_callers can judge callers those tools never list (local functions, indexers, event accessors, compiler backing fields, and <Main>$ appear in none of them; finalizers never appear in get_document_outline); the target symbol's own staticness is irrelevant; unlike find_references / get_diagnostics staticFilter, which also judge an enclosing site but look local functions through to the declaring member and never match top-level statements, find_callers judges a local function as its own calling symbol and counts top-level statements (<Main>$) as static); edge callers: a non-static local function (even inside a static method) is its own calling symbol and counts as instance, while a static local function counts as static; lambdas, including static lambdas, are reported as and judged on the enclosing member; a finalizer is reported as Finalize and counts as instance; an indexer is reported as this[] and judged on the indexer; a call in a custom event accessor (add / remove) is reported as the event and judged on it; an auto-property initializer is reported as the backing field <P>k__BackingField and judged on it (static for a static property); members of a nested type are judged on their own staticness, not the containing type's; a const initializer that references another const is judged on the referencing const (static); top-level statements are reported as the synthesized entry point <Main>$, which is static; combined with the other filters (all must match) and applied before maxResults; a value other than true/false (case-insensitive) is rejected with an error (the MCP tool reports INTERNAL