            "get-code-metrics", "Calculate code metrics (complexity, coupling, etc.); column (optional) disambiguates same-named symbols the same way find_callers does when set with line; omitted keeps today's Line-only / file-level path; column without line keeps today's SymbolResolver omitted-line path");
        r.RegisterQuery<AnalyzeControlFlowOperation, AnalyzeControlFlowParams, AnalyzeControlFlowResult>(
            "analyze-control-flow", "Analyze control flow paths in a method; startColumn / endColumn (optional) trim the region (1-based; Roslyn Character = column - 1); omitted keeps today's whole-line span (start of startLine through end of endLine); result includes EntryPoints (nodes that transfer control into the region from outside, e.g. goto-targeted labels), ExitPoints, ReturnStatements, and reachability flags");
        r.RegisterQuery<AnalyzeDataFlowOperation, AnalyzeDataFlowParams, AnalyzeDataFlowResult>(
            "analyze-data-flow", "Analyze data flow (reads, writes, captures) in a region; startColumn / endColumn (optional) trim the region (1-based; Roslyn Character = column - 1); omitted keeps today's whole-line span (start of startLine through end of endLine)");
        r.RegisterQuery<GetDocumentOutlineOperation, GetDocumentOutlineParams, GetDocumentOutlineResult>(
            "get-document-outline", "Get a structural outline of a C# document; maxDepth (optional, >= 1) drops entries deeper than N (1 = top-level entries only; omit = no depth cap); maxResults (optional) caps the returned outline tree via DFS pre-order after maxDepth (omit = no cap); kindFilter (optional, same values as search-symbols kind-filter, case-insensitive) keeps only entries of that kind plus their containing types/namespaces, applied before maxDepth and maxResults; nameFilter (optional, case-insensitive substring) keeps only entries whose name contains it plus their containing types/namespaces, combined with kindFilter (both must match) and applied before maxDepth and maxResults; accessibilityFilter (optional: public, internal, protected, private, protected internal, or private protected; case-insensitive) keeps only entries with exactly that declared accessibility (implicit defaults count: a top-level type with no modifier is internal, a class member with no modifier is private) plus their containing types/namespaces, combined with kindFilter and nameFilter (all must match) and applied before maxDepth and maxResults; namespaceFilter (optional) keeps only entries declared in that namespace or one nested inside it (ordinal; same matching as search-symbols namespace-filter; namespace entries match on the namespace itself; leading global:: accepted) plus their containing types/namespaces, combined with kindFilter, nameFilter, and accessibilityFilter (all must match) and applied before maxDepth and maxResults; staticFilter (optional boolean) keeps only entries whose declared symbol is static when true (const fields and enum members count as static) or only non-static entries when false, plus their containing types/namespaces (namespaces never match either value; a matching type keeps only its matching children; a non-matching type is kept only as a container for matching descendants); the outline never lists operators (including conversion operators), indexers, finalizers, property/event accessors, local functions, or delegates declared inside a type, so staticFilter can never return them (operators are always static); explicit interface implementations are listed and judged by IsStatic (normally instance; a static abstract interface implementation counts as static), unlike get_symbol_info Members; Like get_symbol_info / search_symbols / find_implementations staticFilter, this judges each entry's declared symbol itself, unlike find_references / find_callers / get_diagnostics staticFilter, which judge the enclosing site symbol of each usage / call / diagnostic; combined with the other filters (all must match) and applied before maxDepth and maxResults; a value other than true/false (case-insensitive) is rejected with an error (the MCP tool reports INTERNAL_ERROR); result includes Truncated when capped");
        r.RegisterQuery<GetSymbolInfoOperation, GetSymbolInfoParams, DetailedSymbolInfo>(
            "get-symbol-info", "Get detailed information about a symbol at a position; kindFilter (optional) same values as search-symbols kind-filter (case-insensitive) keeps only Members of that kind on a type, applied before maxResults; accessibilityFilter (optional) same values as search-symbols accessibility-filter (public, internal, protected, private, protected internal, private protected; case-insensitive) keeps only Members with exactly that declared accessibility (implicit defaults count), combined with kindFilter and applied before maxResults; nameFilter (optional) case-insensitive substring on the member simple name (same matching as get-document-outline name-filter) keeps only Members whose name contains it, combined with kindFilter and accessibilityFilter and applied before maxResults; namespaceFilter (optional) same matching as search-symbols / get-document-outline / find-implementations / get-type-hierarchy / find-references / find-callers / get-diagnostics namespace-filter (ordinal, case-sensitive; containing namespace equals it or is nested inside it; leading global:: accepted; bare global:: filters nothing; global-namespace members never match) keeps only Members in that namespace scope, combined with kindFilter / accessibilityFilter / nameFilter (order: kindFilter → accessibilityFilter → nameFilter → namespaceFilter → staticFilter → maxResults); staticFilter (optional boolean) keeps only static Members when true (const fields count as static) or only instance Members when false (omit = all); Nested types are judged by IsStatic too: a nested static class counts as static; any other nested type (class, struct, enum, interface, delegate, record) counts as instance. Operators (including conversion operators), constructors (including static constructors), indexers, property / event accessors and explicit interface implementations never appear in Members, so staticFilter = true cannot return them (a finalizer ~T() does appear and counts as instance); Like get_document_outline / search_symbols / find_implementations staticFilter, this judges each member's own symbol itself, unlike find_references / find_callers / get_diagnostics staticFilter, which judge the enclosing site symbol of each usage / call / diagnostic; no match gives empty Members, TotalCount = 0, Truncated = false; a value other than true/false (case-insensitive) is rejected with an error (the MCP tool reports INTERNAL_ERROR); Members of a type normally share the type's containing namespace so a named filter typically keeps all or none (e.g. App keeps members of a type in App.Services); for metadata types each member is judged by its own containing namespace; maxResults (optional) caps the returned Members list of a type (omit = no cap); result includes TotalCount and Truncated; Interfaces, Parameters and other fields are not filtered or capped, and kindFilter/accessibilityFilter/nameFilter/namespaceFilter/staticFilter/maxResults have no effect on non-type symbols");

        // ── Query: Type Hierarchy (1) ────────────────────────────────
        r.RegisterQuery<GetTypeHierarchyOperation, GetTypeHierarchyParams, GetTypeHierarchyResult>(
            "get-type-hierarchy", "Get the inheritance hierarchy for a type; maxResults (optional) caps the returned DerivedTypes list (omit = no cap); result includes Truncated when capped; derivedFile (optional) restricts reported DerivedTypes to those declared in that absolute .cs file (applied before maxResults, so totalCount / truncated reflect the filtered set); projectPath (optional) restricts reported DerivedTypes to those declared in documents of one project of the solution by absolute .csproj path (omit = whole solution), applied before maxResults; transitive (optional, default true) set to false returns only direct subclasses instead of every descendant, with derivedFile / projectPath / maxResults applied to that direct set; namespaceFilter (optional) restricts reported DerivedTypes to those whose containing namespace equals it or is nested inside it (ordinal; e.g. App.Services matches App.Services.Orders, not App.ServicesExtra; same matching as search_symbols / find_implementations namespaceFilter), applied before maxResults; accessibilityFilter (optional) public / internal / protected / private / protected internal / private protected (case-insensitive; same values as search-symbols accessibility-filter) keeps only DerivedTypes whose declared accessibility equals it exactly (implicit defaults count), applied before maxResults; kindFilter (optional: a single symbol kind such as Class or Record; case-insensitive; same values as search-symbols / find-implementations kind-filter) keeps only DerivedTypes of that kind (records are Record, not Class), applied before maxResults; nameFilter (optional: ordinal, case-insensitive substring; same matching as get_document_outline / get_symbol_info / find_implementations nameFilter) keeps only DerivedTypes whose simple name contains it, applied before maxResults; abstractFilter (optional boolean; --abstract-filter alone means true) set to true keeps only abstract DerivedTypes (INamedTypeSymbol.IsAbstract: abstract classes and abstract records) and false keeps only concrete, instantiable ones (including sealed classes and records), combined with the other filters (all must match) and applied before maxResults (with transitive false it filters the direct subclasses only); a value other than true/false (case-insensitive) is rejected with an error (the MCP tool reports INTERNAL_ERROR); BaseTypes and Interfaces are not filtered; sourceFile still locates the target type");

        // ── Diagnose (1) — special, no workspace required ────────────
        r.RegisterManual("diagnose",
            "Check the health of the Roslyn environment and workspace status",
            typeof(DiagnoseParams), "Diagnostic",
            (_, json, ct) =>
            {
                // Diagnose is handled specially in Program.cs; this registration
                // exists for help generation and tool listing purposes.
                // The actual execution is in Program.cs since it needs IWorkspaceProvider,
                // not WorkspaceContext.
                throw new InvalidOperationException(
                    "Diagnose is handled directly in Program.cs, not via generic dispatch.");
            },
            requiresWorkspace: false);

        return r;
    }
}
